  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "One millimole $=0.001 \\mathrm{mol}$\r\ni.e. $1 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{mol}$\r\n$\\because 96500 \\mathrm{C}$ is required for $1 \\mathrm{mol}$ of electrons.\r\n$\\therefore 193 \\mathrm{C}$ give $\\frac{193 \\times 1}{96500}=0.002 \\mathrm{mol},$ i.e. $2 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{mol}$ of\r\nelectrons.\r\nThus, value of $n$ in $M^{n+}$ is $=\\frac{0.002}{0.001}=2$\r\nHence, option (b) is the correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
